WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.350
Our CO₂ sensors showed something

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.830
unexpected: which rooms were empty, and

3
00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:06.090
when.

4
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.710
One room was empty most afternoons, and

5
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.690
the head teacher asked whose it was.

6
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.190
The data was about air, but it

7
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.630
told us about people.

8
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.270
Today: data ethics, using a project's

9
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.710
data fairly, safely and honestly.

10
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.400
Sensor data is rarely only about things.

11
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.380
CO₂ and noise show when a

12
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.900
room is full or empty.

13
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.130
A door sensor shows when

14
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.130
someone comes in early.

15
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.650
Put next to a timetable, it

16
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.050
can point to one person.

17
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.140
So ask what the project really needs.

18
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.490
For fresh air: CO₂ per room, and the time.

19
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.040
Not names, not a camera,

20
00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.720
not who sat where.

21
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.750
Every extra piece of data is

22
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.550
more to protect and explain.

23
00:00:58.960 --> 00:00:59.540
Quick check!

24
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.110
A colleague wants a camera in each

25
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.470
classroom, to check the windows get

26
00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:06.830
opened.

27
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:08.390
Is it needed?

28
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.560
No camera needed: when

29
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.700
windows open, the CO₂ falls.

30
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.440
A camera would film children's faces,

31
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.880
which needs far more care and permission.

32
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.590
Choose the least data that

33
00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.350
answers your question.

34
00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.210
Before you start, tell people what you'll

35
00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.950
collect, why, and who will see it.

36
00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.810
For anything about people, ask for

37
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:34.410
consent, and for children, ask their

38
00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.050
parents too.

39
00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.180
Use plain words, in the language

40
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.500
families speak at home.

41
00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.940
Decide who sees what: everyone sees room

42
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:47.020
averages, only the team sees raw readings.

43
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.960
Keep raw data for a term, then delete it.

44
00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.690
Data protection laws in Kenya, Nigeria and

45
00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:58.190
Egypt expect limited access, and no

46
00:01:58.190 --> 00:01:59.890
keeping data longer than you need it.

47
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.510
Then share what you found, honestly.

48
00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.750
Say how sure you are: one sensor per room,

49
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.830
two weeks of data, a gap during exams.

50
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.770
Show the bad news too, and

51
00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.410
what you removed and why.

52
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.860
Room six has the worst air in the

53
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.280
school: that claims too much.

54
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.210
Room six went above fifteen hundred

55
00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.470
ppm on most afternoons we measured:

56
00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.150
that's honest, and still useful.

57
00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:30.940
Your turn.

58
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.410
The head teacher wants the CO₂ data to see

59
00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.070
which teachers leave their rooms early.

60
00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.330
The data could show it.

61
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.320
Should the project hand it over?

62
00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.850
No: people agreed to a project about

63
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.610
fresh air, not about watching staff.

64
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.600
A new use needs new consent.

65
00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.630
Remember: only the data you need, ask

66
00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:56.670
and explain, limit who sees it and for

67
00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.830
how long, and report honestly.

68
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.130
Try it in class tomorrow: a data audit.

69
00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.580
For each piece of data, pupils ask: do

70
00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.920
we need it, what could it reveal, who

71
00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.880
sees it, and when is it deleted?

72
00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.440
Then they write a short

73
00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.700
notice for families.

74
00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.380
Now lead a project your school can trust.
